Chapter: ProbeClosureNocapture

 Do the CAPTURES matter? A definition returning a bare function name still
 goes through emit-partial-application (X86_64.codex:2219 routes a bare
 FunTy name to emit-partial-application st name []), so the inline
 trampoline is still emitted and the closure is still one word -- the code
 pointer -- but nothing is captured and emit-store-closure-captures does
 nothing.

 `tco-bare 47` means captures are required, and the capture store is the
 suspect. A fault means captures are irrelevant and the trampoline or the
 code-pointer word is, which is a much narrower place to look.

 The expected-fine cell is driven first: a fault halts the program.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

 Reached directly, no self call anywhere in the definition.

  give-add3 : Integer -> (Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  give-add3 (n) = add3

 Contains a self tail call, returns the same bare function.

  count-bare : Integer -> (Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  count-bare (n) = if n == 0 then add3 else count-bare (n - 1)

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("direct-bare " & show ((((give-add3 1) 5) 20) 22))
    print-line-uni ("tco-bare " & show ((((count-bare 3) 5) 20) 22))
  end
